    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries an elite 84.88 efficiency score against Bennett. This is our strongest play of the day, bolstered by a 4.88 xERA matchup and a significant park factor boost of +7%. Following him, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.90) offer high-floor utility. Both benefit from favorable matchups against Avila and Whisenhunt, respectively, where their ability to leverage solid lineup positioning\u2014second in the order for both\u2014maximizes their scoring potential. **Jackson Merrill** also remains a core staple today (67.79) as he draws a exploitable matchup against Leahy, maintaining his status as an essential high-upside play.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Brayan Rocchio**, whose 53.93 score fell just shy of the utility threshold. While **Brayan Rocchio** presents a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Cole Carrigg** (65.21), whose switch-hitting profile and favorable matchup against Assad provide more category-wide versatility. We are monitoring **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** closely today; both face McClanahan, whose elite skill set forces a dip in our expectations for them. Despite the tough matchup, **Andy Pages** retains value due to the slow delivery of the opposition, which theoretically improves his chances for a stolen base\u2014our primary metric of concern. \n\nManagers should note that while **Gunnar Henderson** has a strong 65.43 projection, his score is slightly suppressed by the skill of Kirby. We have successfully avoided any extreme weather warnings, but the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several depth pieces suggests we should keep a close eye on late-afternoon announcements. **Nasim Nunez** is a specialized play today; while his score of 54.91 is marginal, his elite sprint speed remains critical to our stolen base strategy, necessitating his inclusion despite the lower-than-average batting order placement.",
